"""Isolated original SchedulerMain plus two Go agents; no legacy lab mutation."""
import argparse
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import re
import secrets
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import zipfile

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
LABEL = 'org.apache.aurora.inplace'
BASE = 'debian:bookworm-slim@sha256:6bd27d44e6c32a66bbd72d7cb2b76a8ae3497ec2e5274a81abd1b37f6013fa1f'
ROLES = ('agent-a', 'agent-b', 'scheduler')


def need(value, message):
    if not value:
        raise ValueError(message)


def safe(path):
    need(path.is_absolute() and '..' not in path.parts and ',' not in str(path), 'Absolute safe path required')
    need(not any(p.is_symlink() for p in (path, *path.parents)), 'Symlink path refused')
    return path


def run(args, timeout=60):
    p = subprocess.run(list(map(str, args)), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)
    if p.returncode:
        raise ValueError('Command failed: ' + str(args[0]) + ': ' + p.stderr[-2000:])
    return p.stdout.strip()


def docker(*args):
    return run(['docker', *args])


def save(root, data):
    path = root / 'lab.json'
    temp = root / 'lab.json.tmp'
    safe(temp)
    with temp.open('w') as f:
        json.dump(data, f, indent=2); f.flush(); os.fsync(f.fileno())
    os.replace(temp, path)
    fd = os.open(root, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
    try: os.fsync(fd)
    finally: os.close(fd)


def digest_tree(root):
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    for p in sorted(root.rglob('*')):
        safe(p)
        need(p.is_dir() or p.is_file(), 'Special artifact refused')
        if p.is_file():
            h.update(str(p.relative_to(root)).encode() + b'\0' + hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).digest())
    return h.hexdigest()


def inspect(data, role, network=False):
    record = data['network'] if network else data['containers'][role]
    ident = record.get('id')
    need(isinstance(ident, str) and re.fullmatch('[a-f0-9]{64}', ident), 'Unknown creation identity; preserved')
    item = json.loads(docker(*(['network', 'inspect'] if network else ['inspect']), ident))[0]
    labels = item.get('Labels', {}) if network else item['Config'].get('Labels', {})
    need(item['Id'] == ident and labels.get(LABEL) == data['token'] and labels.get(LABEL + '.role') == role,
         'Ownership mismatch; resource preserved')
    need(item['Name'].lstrip('/') == record['name'], 'Name mismatch; preserved')
    if network:
        need(item['Internal'] and item['Driver'] == 'bridge', 'Network boundary mismatch')
    else:
        hc = item['HostConfig']
        need(not hc['Privileged'] and hc['ReadonlyRootfs'] and hc['CapDrop'] == ['ALL']
             and hc['NetworkMode'] == data['network']['name'] and not hc.get('PortBindings')
             and hc.get('PidMode', '') == '' and hc.get('SecurityOpt') == ['no-new-privileges:true']
             and item['Config']['User'] == str(data['uid']) + ':' + str(data['gid']), 'Sandbox mismatch; preserved')
        actual = sorted((m['Source'], m['Destination'], m['RW']) for m in item['Mounts'] if m['Type'] == 'bind')
        need(actual == sorted(tuple(m) for m in record['mounts']), 'Mount ownership mismatch; preserved')
        need(item['Config']['Entrypoint'] == ['/opt/bin/cluster-helper'] and item['Config']['Cmd'] == record['args'], 'Command mismatch; preserved')
        need(item['Image'] == data['image'], 'Image mismatch; preserved')
    return item


def prepare(root, args):
    need(not root.exists(), 'New root required; use status/down for existing lab')
    sources = {'scheduler': args.distribution, 'java': args.java, 'helper': args.helper, 'agent': args.agent}
    for p in sources.values(): safe(p); need(p.exists(), 'Missing build artifact: ' + str(p))
    need((args.distribution / 'bin/aurora-scheduler').is_file(), 'Original scheduler distribution required')
    source_hashes = {'agent': digest_tree(ROOT / 'agent'),
                     'helper': digest_tree(ROOT / 'build-support/lab/fixtures/cluster-helper')}
    binaries = {}
    for role in ('agent', 'helper'):
        path = sources[role]
        metadata_path = safe(path.with_name(path.name + '.provenance.json'))
        metadata = json.loads(metadata_path.read_text())
        digest = hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
        need(metadata['sourceSha256'] == source_hashes[role] and metadata['binarySha256'] == digest,
             role + ' source/build provenance mismatch; rebuild current source')
        binaries[role] = metadata
    own_main = False
    for jar in sorted((args.distribution / 'lib').glob('*.jar')):
        safe(jar)
        with zipfile.ZipFile(jar) as archive:
            names = set(archive.namelist())
        own_main |= 'org/apache/aurora/scheduler/app/SchedulerMain.class' in names
        need(not any(n.endswith('/NativeSchedulerMain.class') or n.endswith('/NativeEngine.class') for n in names),
             'Replacement scheduler class refused')
    need(own_main, 'Original SchedulerMain absent from distribution')
    jdk_metadata = {'treeSha256': digest_tree(args.java),
                    'releaseSha256': hashlib.sha256((args.java / 'release').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),
                    'release': (args.java / 'release').read_text()}
    image = json.loads(docker('image', 'inspect', BASE))[0]['Id']
    root.mkdir(parents=True, mode=0o700)
    token = secrets.token_hex(8)
    data = {'schema': 1, 'token': token, 'uid': os.getuid(), 'gid': os.getgid(), 'image': image,
            'prefix': 'aurora-inplace-' + token, 'containers': {}, 'network': None,
            'sourceHashes': source_hashes, 'binaries': binaries, 'jdk': jdk_metadata,
            'schedulerDistributionSha256': digest_tree(args.distribution)}
    save(root, data)
    artifacts = root / 'artifacts'; artifacts.mkdir()
    shutil.copytree(args.distribution, artifacts / 'scheduler')
    shutil.copytree(args.java, artifacts / 'java')
    (artifacts / 'bin').mkdir()
    shutil.copy2(args.helper, artifacts / 'bin/cluster-helper')
    shutil.copy2(args.agent, artifacts / 'bin/aurora-agent')
    need(digest_tree(artifacts / 'scheduler') == data['schedulerDistributionSha256']
         and digest_tree(artifacts / 'java') == jdk_metadata['treeSha256'], 'Artifact changed during staging')
    for role, filename in (('agent', 'aurora-agent'), ('helper', 'cluster-helper')):
        need(hashlib.sha256((artifacts / 'bin' / filename).read_bytes()).hexdigest() == binaries[role]['binarySha256'],
             'Binary changed during staging')
    data['artifactsSha256'] = digest_tree(artifacts); save(root, data)
    for role in ROLES:
        for sub in ('state', 'work', 'control', 'tls', 'config'):
            (root / role / sub).mkdir(parents=True, mode=0o700)
    certs = root / 'certificates'
    run([artifacts / 'bin/cluster-helper', 'certgen', '--out', certs])
    password = secrets.token_hex(24)
    password_file = root / 'scheduler/tls/password'
    password_file.write_text(password); password_file.chmod(0o600)
    run(['openssl', 'pkcs12', '-export', '-name', 'scheduler', '-inkey', certs / 'scheduler.key', '-in', certs / 'scheduler.crt', '-certfile', certs / 'ca.crt', '-out', root / 'scheduler/tls/keystore.p12', '-passout', 'file:' + str(password_file)])
    run([artifacts / 'java/bin/keytool', '-importcert', '-noprompt', '-alias', 'ca', '-file', certs / 'ca.crt', '-keystore', root / 'scheduler/tls/truststore.p12', '-storetype', 'PKCS12', '-storepass:file', password_file])
    nodes = []
    for role in ROLES[:2]:
        for src, dst in [('ca.crt', 'ca.crt'), (role + '.crt', 'cert.crt'), (role + '.key', 'key.pem')]:
            shutil.copy2(certs / src, root / role / 'tls' / dst)
        cfg = {'cluster': 'inplace', 'incarnation': 'recovery-' + token, 'node': role, 'journal': 'journal-' + role,
               'boot': 'boot-' + role, 'runtime': 'runtime-' + role, 'session': 'initial', 'schedulerEpoch': '0',
               'peer': 'scheduler', 'cpuMillis': 1000, 'memoryBytes': 536870912}
        (root / role / 'config/agent.json').write_text(json.dumps(cfg))
        nodes.append({k: cfg[k] for k in ('journal', 'boot', 'runtime', 'cpuMillis', 'memoryBytes')} | {'name': role, 'url': 'https://' + role + ':8443', 'diskMb': 1024})
    config = {'cluster': 'inplace', 'incarnation': 'recovery-' + token, 'database': '/state/adapter.db',
              'keyStore': '/tls/keystore.p12', 'keyStorePassword': password, 'trustStore': '/tls/truststore.p12', 'trustStorePassword': password, 'nodes': nodes}
    (root / 'scheduler/config/scheduler.json').write_text(json.dumps(config))
    (root / 'scheduler/config/scheduler.json').chmod(0o600)
    return data


def up(root, data):
    name = data['prefix'] + '-network'
    data['network'] = {'name': name, 'id': None}; save(root, data)
    ident = docker('network', 'create', '--internal', '--driver', 'bridge', '--label', LABEL + '=' + data['token'], '--label', LABEL + '.role=network', name)
    data['network']['id'] = ident; save(root, data)
    inspect(data, 'network', True)
    for role in ROLES:
        mounts = [(str(root / 'artifacts/bin'), '/opt/bin', False)]
        mounts += [(str(root / role / sub), '/' + sub, sub in ('state', 'work', 'control')) for sub in ('state', 'work', 'control', 'tls', 'config')]
        if role == 'scheduler':
            mounts += [(str(root / 'artifacts/scheduler'), '/opt/scheduler', False), (str(root / 'artifacts/java'), '/opt/java', False)]
            command = ['/opt/scheduler/bin/aurora-scheduler', '-cluster_name=inplace', '-serverset_path=/aurora/inplace', '-zk_in_proc=true', '-zk_endpoints=localhost:2181', '-mesos_master_address=unused', '-go_agent_config=/config/scheduler.json', '-http_port=8081', '-http_authentication_mechanism=NONE']
        else:
            command = ['/opt/bin/aurora-agent', 'serve', '--config', '/config/agent.json', '--state', '/state/state.db', '--work-root', '/work', '--network', 'agent-container', '--listen', ':8443', '--tls-cert', '/tls/cert.crt', '--tls-key', '/tls/key.pem', '--tls-ca', '/tls/ca.crt', '--supervise']
        arguments = ['keeper', '--', *command]
        record = {'id': None, 'name': data['prefix'] + '-' + role, 'mounts': mounts, 'args': arguments}
        data['containers'][role] = record; save(root, data)
        cid = root / (role + '.cid')
        argv = ['create', '--cidfile', str(cid), '--name', record['name'], '--pull', 'never', '--init', '--read-only', '--cap-drop', 'ALL', '--security-opt', 'no-new-privileges:true', '--user', str(data['uid']) + ':' + str(data['gid']), '--network', name, '--network-alias', role, '--pids-limit', '256', '--memory', '1g', '--cpus', '2', '--tmpfs', '/tmp:rw,nosuid,nodev,exec,size=64m,mode=1777', '--label', LABEL + '=' + data['token'], '--label', LABEL + '.role=' + role, '--log-opt', 'max-size=2m', '--log-opt', 'max-file=2']
        if role == 'scheduler': argv += ['--env', 'JAVA_HOME=/opt/java', '--env', 'JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx512m --enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED --illegal-native-access=deny']
        for source, destination, rw in mounts: argv += ['--mount', 'type=bind,source=' + source + ',target=' + destination + ('' if rw else ',readonly')]
        try: docker(*argv, '--entrypoint', '/opt/bin/cluster-helper', data['image'], *arguments)
        finally:
            if cid.exists():
                safe(cid); value = cid.read_text().strip(); need(re.fullmatch('[a-f0-9]{64}', value), 'Invalid creation ID')
                record['id'] = value; save(root, data)
        inspect(data, role)
        docker('start', record['id'])


def refresh_scheduler(root, data, distribution):
    inspect(data, 'scheduler')
    safe(distribution)
    need(distribution.is_dir() and (distribution / 'bin/aurora-scheduler').is_file(), 'Missing scheduler distribution')
    need(not distribution.is_relative_to(root) and not root.is_relative_to(distribution), 'Refresh input must be outside lab')
    original = root / 'artifacts/scheduler'
    need(digest_tree(root / 'artifacts') == data['artifactsSha256'], 'Staged artifact drift; refresh refused')
    own_main = False
    for jar in (distribution / 'lib').glob('*.jar'):
        safe(jar)
        with zipfile.ZipFile(jar) as archive:
            names = set(archive.namelist())
        own_main |= 'org/apache/aurora/scheduler/app/SchedulerMain.class' in names
        need(not any(n.endswith('/NativeSchedulerMain.class') or n.endswith('/NativeEngine.class') for n in names), 'Replacement scheduler refused')
    need(own_main, 'Original SchedulerMain absent')
    expected = digest_tree(distribution)
    staged = root / ('refresh-' + secrets.token_hex(8))
    shutil.copytree(distribution, staged)
    need(digest_tree(staged) == expected, 'Distribution changed while copying')
    control = root / 'scheduler/control'
    need(all(not (control / action).exists() for action in ('pause', 'resume', 'restart', 'crash')), 'Pending keeper action; refresh refused')
    before = json.loads(safe(control / 'daemon.json').read_text())
    data['refreshPending'] = {'oldSha256': data['schedulerDistributionSha256'], 'newSha256': expected, 'staged': str(staged)}
    save(root, data)
    with safe(control / 'pause').open('x') as f: f.write('scheduler artifact refresh\n')
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 15
    while True:
        state = json.loads((control / 'daemon.json').read_text())
        if state.get('paused') is True and state.get('pid') == 0 and not (control / 'pause').exists(): break
        need(time.monotonic() < deadline, 'Keeper did not confirm stopped scheduler; evidence preserved')
        time.sleep(0.1)
    inspect(data, 'scheduler')
    # Keep the bind-mounted directory inode; replace only its verified contents.
    need(digest_tree(original) == data['schedulerDistributionSha256'], 'Scheduler distribution drift')
    for child in original.iterdir():
        if child.is_dir(): shutil.rmtree(child)
        else: child.unlink()
    for child in staged.iterdir(): shutil.move(str(child), original / child.name)
    need(digest_tree(original) == expected, 'Replacement verification failed; scheduler remains paused')
    staged.rmdir()
    data.setdefault('refreshHistory', []).append(data.pop('refreshPending'))
    data['schedulerDistributionSha256'] = expected
    data['artifactsSha256'] = digest_tree(root / 'artifacts')
    save(root, data)
    with safe(control / 'resume').open('x') as f: f.write('scheduler artifact refresh complete\n')
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 15
    while True:
        state = json.loads((control / 'daemon.json').read_text())
        if not state.get('paused') and state.get('pid', 0) > 0 and state.get('generation', 0) > before.get('generation', 0): break
        need(time.monotonic() < deadline, 'Scheduler resume not observed; inspect retained evidence')
        time.sleep(0.1)


def main():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
    p.add_argument('action', choices=['up', 'status', 'restart-scheduler', 'restart-agent', 'crash-scheduler', 'crash-agent', 'refresh-scheduler', 'down'])
    p.add_argument('--root', type=Path, required=True)
    p.add_argument('--node', choices=ROLES[:2], default='agent-a')
    p.add_argument('--distribution', type=Path, default=ROOT / '.cache/inplace-build/build/scheduler/install/aurora-scheduler')
    p.add_argument('--java', type=Path, default=ROOT / '.cache/java03-tools/java/jdk-25.0.4.1+1')
    p.add_argument('--helper', type=Path, default=ROOT / '.pi-tools/agent-original-integration/cluster-helper')
    p.add_argument('--agent', type=Path, default=ROOT / '.pi-tools/agent-original-integration/aurora-agent')
    a = p.parse_args(); root = safe(a.root)
    if a.action == 'up': data = prepare(root, a)
    else:
        need(root.stat().st_uid == os.getuid() and root.stat().st_mode & 0o077 == 0, 'Private owned root required')
        safe(root / 'lab.json'); data = json.loads((root / 'lab.json').read_text())
        need(data['schema'] == 1 and data['uid'] == os.getuid() and re.fullmatch('[a-f0-9]{16}', data['token']) and data['prefix'] == 'aurora-inplace-' + data['token'], 'Invalid ownership record')
    safe(root / '.lock')
    with (root / '.lock').open('a') as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        if a.action != 'up':
            data = json.loads((root / 'lab.json').read_text())
            need(data['schema'] == 1 and data['uid'] == os.getuid() and re.fullmatch('[a-f0-9]{16}', data['token']) and data['prefix'] == 'aurora-inplace-' + data['token'], 'Invalid locked ownership record')
        if a.action == 'up': up(root, data)
        elif a.action == 'down':
            for role in reversed(ROLES):
                if role in data['containers']:
                    inspect(data, role); docker('rm', '-f', data['containers'][role]['id']); del data['containers'][role]; save(root, data)
            if data['network']:
                inspect(data, 'network', True); docker('network', 'rm', data['network']['id']); data['network'] = None; save(root, data)
        elif a.action == 'refresh-scheduler':
            refresh_scheduler(root, data, a.distribution)
        elif a.action != 'status':
            action, target = a.action.split('-'); role = 'scheduler' if target == 'scheduler' else a.node
            inspect(data, role); path = safe(root / role / 'control' / action)
            with path.open('x') as f: f.write('owned request\n')
        result = {'root': str(root), 'containers': {}}
        for role in data['containers']:
            item = inspect(data, role)
            result['containers'][role] = {'id': item['Id'], 'running': item['State']['Running'], 'address': item['NetworkSettings']['Networks'][data['network']['name']]['IPAddress']}
        print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    try: main()
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        print('inplace-cluster: ' + str(e), file=sys.stderr); sys.exit(2)
